    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1298">

                <pb facs="1243" n="1077" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1077"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115R39/5</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Special Representative Rodgers
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-17T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1917, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>216. Department’s July 14, 5 p.m.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d1298-f1"/> Simpich
                    reports interviewing Governor who states Richardson Company’s property was
                    seized because owned by country’s enemies; but now that war is avoided he is
                    ordering administrator to relinquish possession property.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
